  "theorems": [
    "For P=product Z_j and E=sum_j P/Z_j, S_sym=P/gcd(P,(|t|E)^N) has valuation one exactly at t-away singleton incidences for every p>A.",
    "The actual carrier is U_11=gcd(Q^[1],rad_(>A)(S_sym)); its raw symmetric height is at most two beta copies and gives no new capacity bound.",
    "At every actual singleton p, v_p(P)=1 and (P/p)E^(-1)=Z_j/p mod p with 1<=Z_j/p<A, so the top-symmetric first quotient is nonzero.",
    "For P*C(E)/V with V a p-unit, a second p is equivalent to p|C(E).",
    "On a positive-singleton-mass subsequence, E has positive beta height; nonconstant fixed-degree C(E)/D with coefficient and D height b^o cannot be sub-beta."
  ],
